{"title":"Career Roadmap · R&D Executive","role":"R&D Executive","summary":"A Pharmaceutical R&D Executive works on the research, development, optimisation, testing, and documentation of pharmaceutical products and processes.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Pharm (Bachelor of Pharmacy)","Course":"Pharmaceutical Chemistry"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Pharmaceutical R&D Executive works on the research, development, optimisation, testing, and documentation of pharmaceutical products and processes."},{"type":"h","text":"The role can involve:"},{"type":"h","text":"Drug discovery support"},{"type":"h","text":"Pharmaceutical chemistry"},{"type":"h","text":"Formulation development"},{"type":"h","text":"Analytical method development"},{"type":"h","text":"Preformulation studies"},{"type":"h","text":"Stability studies"},{"type":"h","text":"Process optimisation"},{"type":"h","text":"Literature and patent research"},{"type":"h","text":"Laboratory experimentation"},{"type":"h","text":"Documentation and technical reporting"},{"type":"p","text":"A B.Pharm graduate with a Pharmaceutical Chemistry background can enter entry-level R&D roles, although highly specialised discovery, medicinal chemistry, advanced formulation research, or senior scientist positions often require relevant postgraduate education and/or substantial experience."}]},{"heading":"Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"10+2 / Intermediate"},{"type":"h","text":"│"},{"type":"h","text":"├── Physics"},{"type":"h","text":"├── Chemistry"},{"type":"h","text":"└── Biology / Mathematics"},{"type":"h","text":"│"},{"type":"h","text":"▼"},{"type":"h","text":"B.Pharm"},{"type":"h","text":"│"},{"type":"h","text":"▼"},{"type":"h","text":"Pharmaceutical Chemistry /"},{"type":"h","text":"R&D Laboratory Exposure"},{"type":"h","text":"│"},{"type":"h","text":"▼"},{"type":"h","text":"R&D Trainee / Junior"},{"type":"h",